From ebefdff87bc43664fb48524d224019a1c260dc42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: newjordan <newjordan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 03:55:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] sycl: specialize NX2 MoE gate/up, weighted sum, and tail add

Add a default-on exact NX2 fused gate/up SwiGLU path for reordered Q4_K/Q5_K MoE expert GEMV. The default mode fuses only the NX2 ncols=2048, nrows=512, top-k 8 shape: quantize the shared activation row once, compute gate and up dots in one specialized kernel, apply SwiGLU in-kernel, and write the GLU output directly. The retained NX2 reducer uses sycl::reduce_over_group; XOR, alternate SwiGLU activation modes, rowpack scheduling, activation-Q8 caching, expert-pack scheduling, dual-dot vecdot, and Q8 handoff are available only as profiling modes because they measured slower, reversed under repeat, or were too noisy to promote.

Also fuse the exact NX2 post-down weighted expert sum. The graph pass recognizes the F32 [2048,8] down output multiplied by normalized top-k weights and the following seven-add reduction, then writes ffn_moe_out directly in one kernel. The default scalar weighted-sum mode is retained; vec4 row-pack and local-weight variants are present only as explicit profiling modes because they measured slower.

Add a default-on F32 MoE tail-add fusion for the following two-add chain: ffn_moe_out + ffn_moe_shexp, then + ffn_inp. The matcher is shape- and use-count-gated to contiguous NX2 [2048] F32 vectors. Scalar tail-add mode 1 remains default; a vec4 tail-add mode 2 is kept as an opt-in profiling path because the measured result was noisy and not promotion-worthy.

Keep broader direct fusion and shared-Q8 experiments available as explicit profiling modes behind GGML_SYCL_ENABLE_MOE_GATE_UP_FUSION. Mode 3 is the default narrow NX2 path, mode 1 is broad direct fusion, mode 2 is shared-Q8 without direct GLU output, and mode 0 disables gate/up fusion. The weighted-sum, down-weighted-sum, tail-add, and RMS_NORM+MUL fusions have their own gates.

Add separate opt-in probes for shared-expert dense gate/up SwiGLU, activation-Q8 reuse for that shared-expert path, shared-gate-tail scalar, vec4, and local-gate broadcast, shared-gate-sigmoid-tail scalar and vec4, exact Q6_K down projection specialization, Q6_K down-plus-weighted-sum serial/atomic/local-reduce variants, weighted-sum-plus-tail, tail-add+RMS_NORM, standalone RMS_NORM+MUL, post-norm Q8 handoff into MoE gate/up, selective post-norm Q8 handoff, MoE fusion dispatch guarding, alternate gate/up SwiGLU activation lowering, gate/up rowpack scheduling modes 5/6/7, gate/up local-Q8 activation caching, gate/up expert-pack scheduling modes 9/10, gate/up dual-dot vecdot mode 11, gate/up Q8 handoff into the following Q6_K down projection, and weighted-sum local weight caching. They are disabled by default because the retained Q5_K_M ctx0 A/Bs are slower than the default path, below the +2% promotion bar, reversed under repeat, or too noisy to promote.

Validation on Arc Pro B70: targeted MUL_MAT_ID backend-op testing passes 690/690, Q5_K_M ctx0 decode improves from 85.04 to 88.08 t/s (+3.57%) under the retained default, Q4_K_M ctx0 reaches 93.49 t/s, Q5_K_M 131k reaches 42.29 t/s, and Q5_K_M 30-chunk PPL is unchanged at 5.5642 +/- 0.15223. Full backend-op testing retains the known 12 GET_ROWS failures. The default-off shared-expert dense gate/up probe measured 87.27 t/s off versus 86.90 t/s on; activation-Q8 cache for the shared-expert path passed targeted tests but measured 87.76 t/s cache-on versus 88.14 t/s cache-off, then 87.43 versus 87.85 in reverse; the opt-in gate/up XOR reducer measured 87.81 t/s versus 87.96 t/s for the retained reducer; gate/up activation mode 3 measured 87.74 t/s versus 88.06 t/s, and mode 4 measured 87.76 t/s versus a noisy 87.88 t/s retained repeat; gate/up rowpack mode 5 measured 87.70 t/s versus 88.10 t/s for retained mode 1; rowpack modes 6 and 7 passed targeted tests, but mode 6 lost to mode 1 in the reversed Q5 repeat (87.46 versus 87.72 t/s) and Q4 guard (93.53 versus 93.80 t/s), while mode 7 measured 87.64 t/s in the noisy first Q5 pass; gate/up local-Q8 mode 8 passed targeted tests but tied retained mode on Q5_K_M across a reversed repeat (88.20 versus 88.17, then 87.67 versus 87.67 t/s) and regressed Q4_K_M (90.08 versus 93.91 t/s); gate/up expert-pack modes 9 and 10 passed targeted tests, but mode 9 stayed below the Q5_K_M +2% promotion bar across a reversed repeat (88.09 versus 86.83, then 87.13 versus 87.00 t/s), mode 10 trailed at 87.39 t/s, and Q4_K_M mode 9 measured 93.87 versus 92.75 t/s retained; gate/up dual-dot vecdot mode 11 passed targeted tests, but only tied retained Q5_K_M after a reversed repeat (87.59 versus 87.07, then 87.30 versus 87.29 t/s) and regressed Q4_K_M (92.76 versus 94.15 t/s); gate/up Q8 handoff measured 88.02 t/s on versus 87.93 off, then 87.34 on versus 87.56 off in a reversed repeat; exact Q6_K down specialization measured 87.62 t/s versus 87.84 t/s off; Q8 handoff plus exact Q6_K down measured 87.51 t/s versus 87.68 t/s for the retained default; down-weighted-sum mode 1 measured 87.85 t/s versus 87.98 t/s off; atomic mode 2 measured 87.68 t/s versus 88.17 off; local-reduce mode 3 passed targeted tests but measured 87.68 t/s versus 87.99 t/s off; shared-gate-tail scalar measured 88.16 t/s on versus 87.81 off, then 87.83 on versus 87.67 off, with Q4_K_M at 94.22 on versus 92.64 off; shared-gate-tail vec4 measured 87.88 t/s on versus 87.07 off, then 87.80 on versus 87.22 off, with Q4_K_M at 94.43 on versus 92.00 off; shared-gate-tail local-gate broadcast modes 5 and 6 passed targeted tests but measured 87.65 and 87.55 t/s versus 87.81 t/s for the same-run retained default; shared-gate-sigmoid-tail vec4 measured 88.15 t/s on versus 87.18 off, then 87.47 on versus 87.82 off, with Q4_K_M at 94.52 on versus 92.75 off; the opt-in vec4 weighted-sum probe measured 87.91 t/s versus 88.08 t/s for scalar/default; the opt-in local-weight weighted-sum probe measured 87.60 t/s versus 88.06 t/s for scalar/default; the default-off weighted-tail probe measured 87.74 t/s versus 87.98 t/s off; the default-off dispatch guard measured 87.78 t/s versus 88.09 t/s off; tail-add vec4 was noisy enough to keep scalar tail-add as default; tail-add+RMS_NORM measured 86.37 t/s versus 87.95/87.57 off on Q5_K_M while Q4_K_M improved in the single guard pair (92.77 on versus 91.78 off); standalone RMS_NORM+MUL mode 2 measured 89.15/88.97 t/s versus 88.05/87.84 off on Q5_K_M and 95.77 versus 91.28 off on Q4_K_M, with RMS_NORM 21/21, MUL_MAT_ID 690/690, and 5-chunk Q5_K_M WikiText flat at 5.1289 off versus 5.1329 on; and post-norm Q8 handoff mode 3 measured 88.77 t/s versus 87.56 off on Q5_K_M and 95.80 versus 92.37 off on Q4_K_M, with RMS_NORM 21/21, MUL_MAT_ID 690/690, and 5-chunk Q5_K_M WikiText at 5.1402, but remains default-off because Q5_K_M stayed below the +2% promotion bar and trailed standalone mode 2; selective post-norm Q8 handoff mode 4 passed RMS_NORM 21/21 and MUL_MAT_ID 690/690 but measured 87.58/87.48 t/s on Q5_K_M versus 89.01 t/s for same-run mode 2, with Q4_K_M at 94.32 t/s.
